<title><p>The Analytical Engine</p></title>
<epigraph><p>Numbers are the poetry of reason.</p><text-author>Anonymous</text-author></epigraph>
<section><title><p>Chapter One</p><p>Beginnings</p></title>
<p>The engine weaves <emphasis>algebraic patterns</emphasis> just as the Jacquard loom weaves flowers.<a l:href="#n1" type="note">[1]</a></p>
<poem><title><p>Ode to Gears</p></title><stanza><v>Turn, turn, the brass wheel turns,</v><v>and every cog its purpose learns.</v></stanza></poem>
<cite><p>That brain of mine is something more than merely mortal.</p><text-author>A. L.</text-author></cite>
